 "body": {
  "model": "openai/text-embedding-3-small",
  "input": "Why does search-indexer rebuild the index nightly instead of on every catalog write?\n[2025-12-17] standup/dune/2025-12-17: Decided in today's standup: search-indexer will rebuild the index nightly instead of on every catalog write, since incremental updates left stale entries behind after failed writes. [2025-10-16] incident-review/INC-2025-023: Review of INC-2025-023 (search-indexer, 2025-10-13). The root cause was a reindex job that failed silently on a full disk. We decided that reindex jobs will page on failure, because a silent reindex failure left stale results for two days in INC-2025-023. [2025-04-08] standup/cinder/2025-04-08: Reminder that the indexer depends on the catalog.",
  "dimensions": 1536
 },
